<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia retail sales fall 1.8 pct in June.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia retail sales fall 1.8 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales fell 1.8 percent to A$10.395 billion in June, seasonally adjusted, after rising 2.9 percent to A$10.586 billion in May, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In June 1996, retail sales rose 0.3 percent to A$10.221 billion.</p>
<p>In the June quarter, real retail sales at constant average 1989/90 prices fell 0.5 percent to A$25.986 billion, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Analysts median expectations had centred on a rise of around 0.4 percent for June and a gain of 0.1 percent for the quarter.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, June 1997 (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			   June 97   May 97 m/m pct  June 96  y/y pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj    10.40    10.59   -1.8     10.22    +1.7</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	   9.79    10.50   -6.8	9.68    +1.1</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates   10.48    10.46   +0.1     10.25    +2.2</p>
<p>Retail turnover by group percentage change, seasonally adj.</p>
<p>			     June 97	 May 97	June 96</p>
<p>Food retailing	     -0.9	   +3.4	    0.0</p>
<p>Department stores	 -10.5	   +8.0	   -0.4</p>
<p>Clothing, soft goods     -8.2	   +4.8	   -1.2</p>
<p>Household goods	    +0.4	   +2.8	   +2.9</p>
<p>Recreational goods	 +0.2	   -1.2	   +1.7</p>
<p>Other retailing	    -1.6	   +1.6	   -0.6</p>
<p>Hospitality, services    +1.0	   +0.8	   +0.7</p>
<p>Total			  -1.8	   +2.9	   +0.3</p>
</text>
